---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Closing the Planning Gap Between Brands and Factories - Marker">
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-24">
      <a href="/case-studies" class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
        <svg class="mr-1 h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
        </svg>
        All Case Studies
      </a>

      <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Global Apparel Manufacturing</span>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Closing the Planning Gap Between Brands and Factories</h1>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm">
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Company</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Global apparel manufacturer producing for major international brands</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Team</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Manufacturing leadership coordinating across brand customers and factory operations</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Key Challenge</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Brands share little long-range planning information, forcing manufacturers to finance production with limited visibility into future demand</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Challenge</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">This global apparel manufacturer produces for some of the world's largest brands — and bears a disproportionate share of the financial risk in doing so. Manufacturers in the apparel industry effectively act as banks: they finance fabric procurement, production, and shipping before receiving payment, often carrying working capital exposure of $160M to $200M for a billion-dollar-a-year operation. Standard payment terms run 60 to 90 days, with some stretching to six months.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The root cause of this risk is an information gap. Brands share very little long-range planning data with their manufacturing partners. When a brand's leadership changes — which happens every two to four years on average — orders can freeze overnight, leaving the manufacturer with committed materials and no revenue. Poor orchestration among a brand's own internal functions (product development, design, merchandising, planning, and sourcing) compounds the problem, as conflicting signals reach the factory floor.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Manufacturing leadership described sourcing as the function that should act as the "conductor" coordinating everything — but in practice, that coordination was happening through fragmented, one-directional communication.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Marker creates a shared communication layer between brands and their manufacturing partners, making the flow of planning information more structured and visible. Rather than relying on periodic updates that arrive late or not at all, the manufacturer gains real-time visibility into the signals embedded in day-to-day sourcing communication: order cadence shifts, seasonal planning discussions, and early indicators of volume changes.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">When a brand's internal functions send conflicting signals — design requesting samples while planning reduces forecasts — Marker surfaces these discrepancies so both sides can align before commitments are made. For manufacturers managing relationships with multiple brands, each with their own communication style and cadence, Marker normalizes these interactions into a consistent operational view that supports better capacity planning and working capital management.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Real-time visibility into brand planning signals embedded in day-to-day communication, reducing demand forecast surprises</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Conflicting signals from different brand functions surfaced before they reach the production floor</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Normalized view across multiple brand customers, each with different communication patterns and systems</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Better capacity planning and working capital management through earlier access to demand signals</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">See how Marker bridges the information gap between brands and manufacturers.</p>
        <a href="/book-demo" class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2">Book a Demo</a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
